# Raw run artifacts are regenerated per run and mostly noise — EXCEPT the ones a published claim
# rests on. A number quoted in README/CONFIDENCE that cannot be re-derived from a fresh clone is a
# claim, not a measurement, and this repo has already been bitten by exactly that: a stale
# schema-tax artifact was quoted for months as though it described the shipping default.
# Keep the artifacts behind load-bearing claims; ignore the rest.
raw/*
!raw/schema-tax.json
!raw/compiled-suite-vs-replay.json
!raw/suite-rre.json
!raw/leak-stress.json
!raw/stress-tiers.json
# The text each tool actually returned, per cell. Kept by the rule stated above and for the sharpest
# case of it: this benchmark makes claims about COMPETITORS' detection, and the first time one of
# those moved it was our grader that was wrong, not the tool. A competitor's score that cannot be
# checked against what it actually said is an accusation rather than a measurement.
!raw/observation-evidence.json
logs/
# Ignore run artifacts, but keep the two SVGs embedded in docs/benchmarks.md so the flagship doc
# renders on a fresh clone (they were previously broken image links).
artifacts/*
!artifacts/chart-detection.svg
!artifacts/chart-avg-tokens.svg

# benchmark run artifacts (regenerated per run)
results-*.json
results*.json
pw-vs-reticle/results*.json
pw-vs-reticle/SCORECARD*.md
pw-vs-reticle/MASTER-SCORECARD.md

# local API keys — never committed
.env

# logs / OS cruft
*.log
.DS_Store
